        <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A syndrome characterized by blepharophimosis, blepharoptosis, highly arched eyebrows hypertelorism, cleft lip and palate, postnatal growth deficiency, cognitive impairment, hearing loss and, in a smaller percentage of cases, craniosynostosis, radioulnar synostosis and genital and vesicorenal anomalies. It encompasses four disorders that were previously designated the Malpuech, Michels, Mingarelli and Carnevale syndromes.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <dc:type rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/ECO_0007645"/>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>url:https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/16096999</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
