    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_0060453">
        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">An epithelial-stromal TGFBI dystrophy that is characterized by recurrent erosions and irregular geographic opacification located_in the cornea, proteinaceous deposits in the anterior stroma and subepithelium, and progressive early vision loss, and has_material_basis_in heterozygous mutation of transforming growth factor beta-induced gene located in chromosome 5q31.1, which encodes keratoepithelin. Abnormalities lead to increased protein deposition and disruption especially of Bowman&apos;s membrane of the cornea.</obo:IAO_0000115>
